    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <!-- Header -->
        <div class="report-header">
            <h1>Chocolate Retail Sales Performance Report</h1>
            <div class="subtitle">Comprehensive Analysis of Sales, Profitability, and Customer Behavior</div>
            <div class="subtitle">Fiscal Years 2023–2024</div>
            <div class="date">Report Generated: {datetime.now().strftime('%B %d, %Y')}</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Executive Summary -->
        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
                <p>Key performance indicators and high-level findings for the 2023–2024 period</p>
            </div>

            <div class="kpi-dashboard">
                <div class="kpi-card">
                    <div class="label">Total Revenue</div>
                    <div class="value">${total_revenue:,.0f}</div>
                    <div class="sub-value">+{yoy_growth:.1f}% YoY Growth</div>
                </div>
                <div class="kpi-card">
                    <div class="label">Total Profit</div>
                    <div class="value">${total_profit:,.0f}</div>
                    <div class="sub-value">{avg_profit_margin:.1f}% Avg Margin</div>
                </div>
                <div class="kpi-card highlight">
                    <div class="label">Avg Profit Margin</div>
                    <div class="value">{avg_profit_margin:.1f}%</div>
                    <div class="sub-value">Healthy margin maintained</div>
                </div>
                <div class="kpi-card">
                    <div class="label">Avg Order Value</div>
                    <div class="value">${avg_order_value:.2f}</div>
                    <div class="sub-value">{total_orders:,} total orders</div>
                </div>
                <div class="kpi-card highlight">
                    <div class="label">Discount Utilization</div>
                    <div class="value">{discount_utilization:.1f}%</div>
                    <div class="sub-value">of orders received discount</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="exec-grid">
                <div>
                    <h3 style="margin-bottom: 15px; color: #2E4057;">Key Highlights</h3>
                    <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0;">
                        <li style="padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #ecf0f1;">
                            <strong>Revenue Performance:</strong> Generated ${total_revenue:,.0f} in total revenue across {total_orders:,} transactions
                        </li>
                        <li style="padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #ecf0f1;">
                            <strong>Profitability:</strong> Achieved ${total_profit:,.0f} in total profit with a {avg_profit_margin:.1f}% average margin
                        </li>
                        <li style="padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #ecf0f1;">
                            <strong>Peak Performance:</strong> {month_names[int(peak_month_2024['month'])-1]} 2024 was the strongest month with ${peak_month_2024['revenue']:,.0f} in revenue
                        </li>
                        <li style="padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #ecf0f1;">
                            <strong>Store Network:</strong> {num_stores} stores across the network, with Store {top_store['store_id']} leading at ${top_store['revenue']:,.0f}
                        </li>
                        <li style="padding: 10px 0;">
                            <strong>Product Portfolio:</strong> {top_product_count} products in active catalog, with top product generating ${top_product['revenue']:,.0f}
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="highlight-stat">
                    <div class="number">+{yoy_growth:.1f}%</div>
                    <div class="label">Year-over-Year<br>Revenue Growth</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Sales Trends Over Time -->
        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2>Sales Trends Over Time</h2>
                <p>Monthly and quarterly revenue and order volume trends across 2023 and 2024</p>
            </div>

            <h3 style="margin: 20px 0 15px; color: #2E4057;">Monthly Revenue & Order Trends</h3>
            <div class="chart-container">
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['monthly_trend']}" alt="Monthly Revenue and Order Trends">
            </div>

            <h3 style="margin: 30px 0 15px; color: #2E4057;">Quarterly Performance Comparison</h3>
            <div class="chart-container">
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['quarterly']}" alt="Quarterly Performance">
            </div>

            <div class="insight-box">
                <h4>Seasonality Observations</h4>
                <p>
                    The data reveals distinct seasonality patterns with notable peaks around holiday periods. 2024 shows consistent improvement over 2023 across most months,
                    demonstrating positive momentum. The highest revenue months align with Valentine's Day (February) and winter holiday seasons (November-December).
                    Order volume remains relatively stable month-to-month with slight increases during peak shopping periods.
                </p>
            </div>

            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Metric</th>
                        <th>2023</th>
                        <th>2024</th>
                        <th>Change</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Total Revenue</td>
                        <td>${yearly_revenue.get(2023, 0):,.0f}</td>
                        <td>${yearly_revenue.get(2024, 0):,.0f}</td>
                        <td>+{yoy_growth:.1f}%</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Peak Month</td>
                        <td>{month_names[int(monthly[monthly['year']==2023].loc[monthly[monthly['year']==2023]['revenue'].idxmax(), 'month'])-1]}</td>
                        <td>{month_names[int(peak_month_2024['month'])-1]}</td>
                        <td>—</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Lowest Month</td>
                        <td>{month_names[int(monthly[monthly['year']==2023].loc[monthly[monthly['year']==2023]['revenue'].idxmin(), 'month'])-1]}</td>
                        <td>{month_names[int(low_month_2024['month'])-1]}</td>
                        <td>—</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        <!-- Product & Category Performance -->
        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2>Product & Category Performance</h2>
                <p>Analysis of product-level revenue and profitability across the portfolio</p>
            </div>

            <div class="chart-container">
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['product']}" alt="Top Products by Revenue and Profit">
            </div>

            <h3 style="margin: 30px 0 15px; color: #2E4057;">Top 10 Products by Revenue</h3>
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Product ID</th>
                        <th>Revenue</th>
                        <th>Profit</th>
                        <th>Profit Margin</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    {''.join([f"<tr><td>{row['product_id']}</td><td>${row['revenue']:,.2f}</td><td>${row['profit']:,.2f}</td><td>{row['profit_margin']:.1f}%</td></tr>" for _, row in top_10_products.iterrows()])}
                </tbody>
            </table>

            <div class="insight-box">
                <h4>Product Portfolio Insights</h4>
                <p>
                    The product portfolio demonstrates strong performance across the top 10 products, which collectively drive a significant portion of total revenue.
                    Profit margins remain healthy across the product range, indicating effective pricing strategy and cost management.
                    Product performance is fairly distributed across the catalog, suggesting no over-reliance on single products.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Store & Geographic Performance -->
        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2>Store & Geographic Performance</h2>
                <p>Comparison of sales performance across stores and locations</p>
            </div>

            <div class="chart-container">
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['store']}" alt="Top and Bottom Stores by Revenue">
            </div>

            <h3 style="margin: 30px 0 15px; color: #2E4057;">Top 10 Stores by Revenue</h3>
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Store ID</th>
                        <th>Revenue</th>
                        <th>Profit</th>
                        <th>Orders</th>
                        <th>Avg Order</th>
                        <th>Margin</th>
                    </tr>
